1. CMS public data
The files in v1/data_clean/cms are parsed from the Marketplace public use files
published by the Centers for Medicare and Medicaid Services (Transparency in
Coverage, Plan Attributes and Machine-readable URL files, plan year 2026). These
are U.S. federal public data. The raw files are not redistributed; retrieval
times and SHA-256 hashes are in v1/data_raw/provenance/manifest.csv.

2. Issuer provider files
v1/data_clean/ortho holds counts derived from the machine-readable provider files
that issuers publish for CMS. Only NPI-level tabulations (distinct counts per plan)
and a vocabulary of specialty labels were kept. No clinician names, addresses or
other personal details are stored in this repository, and the individual provider
files are not redistributed.

3. NPI Registry
A stratified sample of NPIs was checked against the public NPI Registry API
(https://npiregistry.cms.hhs.gov/api/). Only taxonomy-code tabulations are kept.

4. NUCC Health Care Provider Taxonomy
v1/config/ortho_taxonomy.csv lists the 22 taxonomy codes (orthopaedic, dermatology
and ophthalmology families) and their display names used for identification. The
code set is maintained by the National Uniform Claim Committee (https://nucc.org,
version 26.1). Obtain the full code set from the NUCC.

5. KFF
The KFF brief on claims denials and appeals in ACA Marketplace plans in 2024 was
used as the replication benchmark. No KFF data file is redistributed; the
comparison is in v1/qa/g2_reconciliation.md.
